From: Florian Fuchs <fuchsfl@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pvr2fb: hide the VRAM clear and set the mode before fbcon

On real hardware the boot shows about a second of blue/black stripes
over the BIOS licence screen before the console appears.

pvr2fb_common_init() clears all 8 MiB of VRAM with fb_memset_io() while
the display is still scanning out with the mode the bootloader set up.
On SH, memset_io() is a loop of writeb(), and the PowerVR2 VRAM does not
handle byte writes, so the "clear" leaves junk on screen. It is also slow:
8M barriered byte writes over the PVR bus take about as long as the
glitch lasts. Only after register_framebuffer(), with fbcon already
drawing, does pvr2_init_display() program the real mode.

Blank the display with a black border before touching VRAM, clear it
with 32-bit writes, and program the mode before registering the
framebuffer, so nothing is scanned out in the stale mode.

Signed-off-by: Florian Fuchs <fuchsfl@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/pvr2fb.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/pvr2fb.c
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/pvr2fb.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/pvr2fb.c
@@ -797,7 +797,7 @@
 static int __maybe_unused pvr2fb_common_init(void)
 {
 	struct pvr2fb_par *par = currentpar;
-	unsigned long modememused, rev;
+	unsigned long modememused, rev, i;
 
 	fb_info->screen_base = ioremap(pvr2_fix.smem_start,
 					       pvr2_fix.smem_len);
@@ -814,7 +814,17 @@
 		goto out_err;
 	}
 
-	fb_memset_io(fb_info->screen_base, 0, pvr2_fix.smem_len);
+	/*
+	 * The display still scans out whatever the bootloader left set up.
+	 * Blank it with a black border until pvr2_init_display() takes over,
+	 * so the VRAM clear below is not visible.
+	 */
+	fb_writel(0, DISP_BRDRCOLR);
+	fb_writel(fb_readl(DISP_DIWCONF) | BLANK_BIT, DISP_DIWCONF);
+
+	/* VRAM does not take byte writes, so clear it a word at a time */
+	for (i = 0; i < pvr2_fix.smem_len; i += 4)
+		fb_writel(0, fb_info->screen_base + i);
 
 	pvr2_fix.ypanstep	= nopan  ? 0 : 1;
 	pvr2_fix.ywrapstep	= nowrap ? 0 : 1;
@@ -837,10 +847,15 @@
 
 	fb_alloc_cmap(&fb_info->cmap, 256, 0);
 
+	/*
+	 * Must write PIXDEPTH to register before anything is displayed, so
+	 * program the mode before fbcon attaches and starts drawing.
+	 */
+	pvr2fb_set_par(fb_info);
+	pvr2_init_display(fb_info);
+
 	if (register_framebuffer(fb_info) < 0)
 		goto out_err;
-	/*Must write PIXDEPTH to register before anything is displayed - so force init */
-	pvr2_init_display(fb_info);
 
 	modememused = get_line_length(fb_info->var.xres_virtual,
 				      fb_info->var.bits_per_pixel);
